  <participating-org ref="NL-KVK-27108436" role="4" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam Novib</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam is working in Senegal since 1981 and has opened a first office in Senegal in 1983. Oxfam in Senegal is implementing a 5-year country strategy (2015-2019) which is articulated around the following vision which is:

Senegal has an active citizenry,comprising of a good representation of men, women and youth, that is willing and capable of influencing the development and implementation of national policies, and receives a more equitable share of the national wealth.

The country strategy uses a two-tiered approach:
-          to promote citizen participation in policy formulation and implementation processes;
-              To promote innovativefield programming that addresses the immediate needs of the poorest segments of society while strengthening their capacity to influence local authorities.

This strategy focusses on sustainable livelihoods, promoting good governance and humanitarian (contributingto strengthening the leadership of local actors in the context of integrated disaster management, from prevention to emergency response). It also recognizes the under-utilized potentialities and power of some marginalized groups, especially women and youth.

Oxfam in Senegal adheres to six partnership principles: shared vision and values,mutual accountability, complementarity, clarity of roles, institutional autonomy, and commitment to joint learning, and is carrying out projects through partnering with local NGOs and organisations (such as producer#s organisations).</narrative>
  </participating-org>
